Dear Dr Rawat,

Your manuscript "Keeping the House in the Family: Non-Market Transfers and =
the Supply of American Homes" has now been assessed. Regrettably, after car=
eful consideration, we have decided not to send your paper for external pee=
r review. We do not believe there is a good match between the manuscript an=
d the Journal of Real Estate Finance and Economics. We do not find the marg=
inal contribution of the paper to the existing body of knowledge significan=
t enough to warrant publication in the Journal. The paper documents an inte=
resting aspect of transactions in housing markets. However, it fails to con=
vince the reader about the significance of this exercise. As you mention in=
 the paper, these non-market transactions would lead to inefficient allocat=
ion of these houses. What I would suggest is that you zoom more into this i=
nefficiency and try to measure the subsequent efficiency / welfare losses. =
This would make the paper more relevant for policy makers.

As an editor, these decisions are never easy but given that we can only acc=
ept a limited number of submissions, our selection process is highly compet=
itive. Consequently, I strive to maximize the efficient use of referees' va=
luable time and to respect your time as well. Therefore, I think it is best=
 to avoid a review process that is unlikely to lead to publication.

This decision should not be taken as a final assessment of the value added =
by your paper, but rather as an effort to facilitate the timely turnaround =
of submissions. Given our low acceptance rate, we must decline many excelle=
nt papers.

Thank you for the opportunity to review your work. I'm sorry that we cannot=
 be more positive on this occasion and hope you will not be deterred from s=
ubmitting future work to The Journal of Real Estate Finance and Economics.


Kind regards,

Abdullah Yavas
Editor
The Journal of Real Estate Finance and Economics

Transfer recommendation

While I'm sorry we cannot publish your work in The Journal of Real Estate F=
inance and Economics, your manuscript may be a good fit for one of our othe=
r journals.


What=E2=80=99s next

At Springer Nature we provide a free service to give authors a range of per=
sonalised journal recommendations. The submitting author will receive a not=
ification with more information shortly.
If you decide to proceed with this option and transfer your manuscript to a=
 different journal, the details from your previous submission will be retai=
ned, making the process faster.

